      "text": "To determine the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by \\(6\\), we start by identifying the sequence and its properties.\n\nThis is an arithmetic sequence where:\n- The first term \\(a\\) is \\(1\\),\n- The common difference \\(d\\) is \\(6\\),\n- The last term \\(l\\) is \\(259\\).\n\n### Step 1: Determine the number of terms (\\(n\\))\n\nFirst, we use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\\[\na_n = a + (n-1)d\n\\]\nWe know \\(a_n = 259\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(d = 6\\):\n\\[\n259 = 1 + (n-1) \\times 6\n\\]\nSolving for \\(n\\):\n\\[\n259 = 1 + 6(n-1)\n\\]\n\\[\n258 = 6(n-1)\n\\]\n\\[\nn-1 = \\frac{258}{6} = 43\n\\]\n\\[\nn = 44\n\\]\n\nSo the sequence contains \\(44\\) terms.\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the sum of the sequence\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2}(a + l)\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(l = 259\\):\n\\[\nS_{44} = \\frac{44}{2}(1 + 259)\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{44} = 22 \\times 260\n\\]\n\\[\nS_{44} = 5720\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the remainder when the sum is divided by 6\n\nFinally, we calculate the remainder when \\(5720\\) is divided by \\(6\\):\n\\[\n5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ R } 2\n\\]\nThus, the remainder is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
